# NPM Configuration for AWS CodeArtifact
# This file is a template - do NOT commit with actual credentials

# Uncomment and configure these settings to use AWS CodeArtifact
# Replace placeholders with your actual values

# registry=https://[DOMAIN]-[ACCOUNT_ID].d.codeartifact.[REGION].amazonaws.com/npm/[REPOSITORY]/
# //[DOMAIN]-[ACCOUNT_ID].d.codeartifact.[REGION].amazonaws.com/npm/[REPOSITORY]/:always-auth=true

# Example:
# registry=https://my-domain-123456789012.d.codeartifact.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/npm/my-repo/
# //my-domain-123456789012.d.codeartifact.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/npm/my-repo/:always-auth=true

# Note: Authentication token should be set via environment variable or AWS CLI
# Do NOT hardcode credentials in this file
# Use: aws codeartifact get-authorization-token --domain my-domain --query authorizationToken --output text

# For local development, you can set the auth token temporarily:
# npm config set //[DOMAIN]-[ACCOUNT_ID].d.codeartifact.[REGION].amazonaws.com/npm/[REPOSITORY]/:_authToken=[TOKEN]

# For CI/CD (AWS CodeBuild), the buildspec.yml handles authentication automatically
